  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 3269ab77e5738674b9fefab358f453ff, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::UIAnimLab.Station
  Code: 
  Title: 11  Edge Cases and Warnings
  Summary: 'Things that go wrong on purpose: warnings in play mode, a property that
    throws, a stencil Mask, a Layout Group, steps that fight, a destroyed object
    mid-play, two components of one type, and a check that every step type still
    has the number it was saved with.


    <b>Using this board:</b> select a tile.
    Its Inspector shows these directions at the top, with Select buttons for the
    objects to watch, and its UI Animation Player underneath. Badges in a tile''s
    corner say what it needs: <color=#FF9E5E>PREVIEW</color> (the Play buttons, out
    of play mode), <color=#FF9E5E>PLAY MODE</color>, <color=#FF9E5E>INSPECTOR</color>,
    <color=#FF9E5E>SCENE VIEW</color>, <color=#FF9E5E>CONSOLE</color>, <color=#FF9E5E>POP-OUT</color>
    (an animation''s own window).


    In play mode: right-drag pans, the wheel
    zooms, Tab steps through tiles, Home shows them all.'
  Watch: 
  WatchObjects: []
  HowTo: 
  Expect: 
  Needs: 0
  Style: 2
  WikiPage: 
